## std::iter — retired.
##
## The `Iterator` (`next`) and `FromIterator` (`from_iter`) mixins were
## vestigial after the Ruby-surface migration removed the iterator layer:
## `Array` has no `.iter` / `.collect` / `from_iter`, and the block
## combinators (`each` / `map` / `select` / `reduce` / `each_with_index` /
## …) work directly on `Array` and are inlined at the MIR layer — they do
## not dispatch through an `Iterator` mixin. With no required-method
## contract to enforce and no user impls, both mixins are removed.
##
## This module is intentionally empty; it is kept as a bootstrap entry so
## `std.iter` remains a resolvable (no-op) namespace. Collections are Ruby
## `Enumerable`-shaped — see docs/specs/syntax/ruby-naming.spec.md.
